Exp 2a:To print Marks above 60

Aim:
To write a Java program to print the marks that are above 60 using an array.

Algorithm:
1. Start the program.
2. Import the Scanner package.
3. Read the number of students.
4. Read the marks of each student.
5. Check whether each mark is greater than 60.
6. Print the marks above 60.
7. Stop the program.

Program:
import java.util.Scanner;
public class MarksAbove60 {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);

        int n, i;
        System.out.print("Enter number of students: ");
        n = sc.nextInt();

        int marks[] = new int[n];

        System.out.println("Enter student marks:");
        for (i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            marks[i] = sc.nextInt();
        }

        System.out.println("Marks above 60:");
        for (i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            if (marks[i] > 60) {
                System.out.println(marks[i]);
            }
        }

        sc.close();
    }
}

